Ethanol/Nutrition/Herb Interactions

Ethanol: May increase CNS depression; monitor for

increased effects with coadministration. Caution patients
about effects.
Food: Carbamazepine serum levels may be increased if

taken with food. Carbamazepine serum concentration
may be increased if taken with grapefruit juice; avoid
concurrent use.
Herb/Nutraceutical : Avoid evening primrose (seizure

threshold decreased). Avoid valerian , St John's wort,
kava kava, gotu kola (may increase CNS depression).
